      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To report previously underrecognized postdosing side effects of methotrexate (MTX)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Over a one and a half year period, in 2 practices, all patients with rheumatoid arthritis (RA) receiving weekly MTX, and volunteering symptoms within a few hours of MTX dosing were carefully questioned concerning the nature of the postdosing reaction."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Of 356 patients, 36 (10%) reported a previously underemphasized postdosing reaction consisting of arthralgias/myalgias, fatigue/malaise or both. Sixteen patients discontinued MTX primarily because of this side effect."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "In these patient populations, postdosing reactions were the 2nd most common side effect (after gastrointestinal) leading to MTX withdrawal."
        }
      ]},
